If you only have Saturdays and Sundays, you will not realistically "master" Python in 30 days. However, you can become job-ready at the beginner-to-intermediate level in about 8 weekends (16 study days) if you focus intensely and use AI effectively.

Weekend Learning Plan (8–10 hours/day)
Weekend 1: Python Fundamentals

Saturday

Install Python and VS Code
Variables, strings, numbers
Input/output
Basic exercises

Sunday

Conditions (if, elif, else)
Loops (for, while)
20 practice problems

AI prompts:

"Give me 20 beginner Python problems."
"Explain loops with visual examples."
Weekend 2: Functions and Data Structures

Saturday

Functions
Parameters and return values

Sunday

Lists
Dictionaries
Sets and tuples

Project:

Student grade manager

AI prompt:

"Review my solution and tell me what's wrong without giving the answer."

Weekend 3: File Handling and OOP

Saturday

Reading/writing files
Exception handling

Sunday

Classes and objects
Inheritance

Project:

Library management system
Weekend 4: Real Projects

Build:

Expense tracker
Password generator
To-do app

Focus:

Writing complete programs
Organizing code into functions
Weekend 5: APIs and Automation

Learn:

HTTP requests
JSON
Working with APIs

Project:

Weather application
News fetcher

Useful documentation:

Requests Library Documentation
Weekend 6: Databases and Git

Learn:

SQLite basics
Git and GitHub

Resources:

GitHub Docs
SQLite Documentation

Project:

Expense tracker with database
Weekend 7: Build One Serious Project

Choose one:

Blog API using FastAPI
Inventory management system
Chat application
Task manager

Use AI as your senior developer.

Weekend 8: Polish and Portfolio
Refactor code
Add README files
Upload everything to GitHub
Learn basic interview questions

Portfolio should contain:

Calculator
To-do app
Expense tracker
API project
Database project
One major project
What to do on weekdays (15 minutes/day)

Even if you can't study, do one of these:

Solve 1 coding problem
Read 2–3 pages of Python docs
Ask AI to explain one concept
Review your weekend code

Fifteen minutes a day adds up to almost 2 extra weekends of learning over a month.

Best way to use AI

Don't ask:

"Write the project for me."

Ask:

"I'm learning Python. Act as a tutor. Give me one task at a time, check my code, and increase the difficulty when I succeed."

That forces you to think and learn rather than copy.